// version.nv — the product's own name and version.
//
// This module is PURE on purpose: it returns the string and prints nothing.
// `println` cannot be called from here — registry defect №1017 (К1, tag blocker):
// `nova check` accepts it, codegen refuses it in every unit that imports the
// module. The class is narrow, and knowing that matters when writing the rest of
// the app: ONLY the two prelude variadics `print` and `println` are affected.
// `panic`, `assert`, `Option`/`Result` do work in a library module, so error
// signalling belongs where it happens; only formatting output has to travel out
// as a value. Repro, spec citation and the narrowing: docs/reports/T0.0.md.
//
// Declaration form differs by depth, and the compiler is the authority here:
// a file DIRECTLY in the source root carries the package name
// (`claude_limits.version`), while a file in a subdirectory does not
// (`bin/claude_limits.nv` is `bin.claude_limits`). Both were learned from
// E_D78_MODULE_PATH_MISMATCH on T0.0, not from memory.

module claude_limits.version

/// Version line printed by the bare binary. Exported so the peer test asserts the
/// exact string T0.0's acceptance greps for, instead of re-typing it.
export fn version_line() -> str => "claude-limits 0.0.0"
